WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.760
With the Eternals headed to the silver screen,&nbsp;
the sorceress known as Sersi is about to become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.280
a big deal to Marvel fans. But who is this&nbsp;
ancient superhero, and what's her story?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.920
From the Odyssey to the Avengers, this is&nbsp;
the history of Marvel's Sersi explained.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:22.400
The first run of Eternals begins with Ikaris on&nbsp;
an expedition with a scientist named Daniel Damian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:27.760
and his daughter, Margo. Ikaris explains the&nbsp;
threat posed by the race known as the Deviants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.280
who, like the Eternals, were&nbsp;
created by the Celestials.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.520
But where the Eternals are good, powerful,&nbsp;
and kind, the Deviants are cruel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.320
hideous, and prone to mutation. Knowing a&nbsp;
war is coming, Ikaris takes Margo to Sersi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.840
so that she might keep the mortal girl&nbsp;
safe in her chic Manhattan apartment.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.880
Sersi agrees to do so, and proceeds to blow&nbsp;
Margo's mind by reminiscing about the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.040
she turned Odysseus' crew into pigs —&nbsp;
as well as the time she taught Merlin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.840
during her stint at King Arthur's court.&nbsp;
Margo is, of course, floored by all this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.560
especially since Sersi appears to be little more&nbsp;
than a gal-about town who's prone to practicing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.120
her dance moves during idle hours at home. When&nbsp;
the Deviants attack her apartment, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.560
Sersi further reveals her skills as a warrior,&nbsp;
barraging her foes with cosmic energy, blocking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:18.080
their blasts of flame, and transforming them all&nbsp;
into animals. Old habits die hard, apparently.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:24.240
Sersi is legendary for her parties — and these&nbsp;
shindigs aren't just fun, either, as they often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.880
serve the plot of the stories in which they&nbsp;
appear. For example, during one particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:34.960
raucous gathering, Sersi is introduced to Marvel&nbsp;
heroes such as the Wasp, She-Hulk, and Starfox,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.920
who she learns is a fellow Eternal. The party is&nbsp;
interrupted when the Eternals attempt to summon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:45.120
her to participate in the Uni-Mind, a kind of&nbsp;
merging of their souls, but she ignores it.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:51.040
Undaunted, the Eternals known as the Delphan&nbsp;
Brothers crash the party. Sersi is made to join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.440
the Uni-Mind, which results in the Eternals&nbsp;
deciding to leave Earth. Sersi refuses to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.760
go along with this, however, as she enjoys&nbsp;
living among humans way too much to leave.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.880
This encounter puts Sersi on the Avengers' radar.&nbsp;
When Captain America needs help finding a bunch of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:11.680
kids in 1989's Captain America #355, he turns&nbsp;
to Sersi to transform him into a teenager.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.400
Later, in Avengers #314, she actually&nbsp;
joins the Avengers at Cap's invitation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.520
It just goes to show you: One&nbsp;
great party can change everything.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.114
"Avengers… A-"

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:29.200
After the Eternal and Avenger known as Gilgamesh&nbsp;
is severely injured, his teammates turn to Sersi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.160
to help heal him. His condition is beyond her&nbsp;
abilities to fix, but she does later agree to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:39.360
join the Avengers in his absence. Facing the&nbsp;
space pirate Nebula in her first mission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:44.400
Sersi saves the team from total obliteration&nbsp;
and helps restore reality in the process.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.960
For a while, things go swimmingly for Sersi.&nbsp;
She handles Mother Night's brainwashing tricks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:54.240
banishes radioactive foes alongside Thor,&nbsp;
and helps a demon called the Unspeakable One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.240
merge with his literal better half.&nbsp;
All along, Sersi remains her bubbly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.960
whip-smart self, and she proves to be a major&nbsp;
team asset, despite how different she is from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:07.120
the rest of the Avengers. In short, Sersi&nbsp;
loves the heroics, she loves the people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.840
and she's awfully good at saving the day. But all&nbsp;
that changes in her next mission as an Avenger.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:19.360
In a storyline beginning with 1991's Avengers&nbsp;
#334, the team faces an alien race called the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:24.320
Brethren, led by the charismatic Thane&nbsp;
Ector. Soon after capturing Sersi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:29.040
Thane Ector falls in love with her, and she&nbsp;
too realizes they have a mysterious connection.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.120
It is later revealed that the Brethren&nbsp;
are also creations of the Celestials,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.680
and the Collector, an old Avengers foe,&nbsp;
is manipulating them to destroy Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.040
Sersi forms the Uni-Mind with the&nbsp;
Brethren to defeat the Collector,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.600
despite the fact that forming the Uni-Mind&nbsp;
with another species is forbidden to Eternals.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.800
Sersi's behavior changes in the aftermath of this&nbsp;
event. She becomes more violent and unstable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:54.240
even as she starts to fall for&nbsp;
her fellow Avenger, Dane Whitman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:59.200
Things are thrown into outright chaos when the&nbsp;
Avengers get involved in a huge interstellar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.520
war between the Kree and Shi'ar, which&nbsp;
turns out to be a ruse concocted by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:06.880
Kree's Supreme Intelligence. When&nbsp;
the Avengers learn of this plot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.600
a breakaway group — including Sersi — kills&nbsp;
him. And this tears the Avengers apart.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.600
Complicating things further, Dane develops&nbsp;
feelings for new teammate Crystal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:20.880
and against his better judgment, starts a romance&nbsp;
with Sersi, too. This does little to calm Sersi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.440
who soon grows even more troubled. When the team&nbsp;
travels to a distant dimension and fails to stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:30.240
a young girl from being sacrificed by a priest,&nbsp;
Sersi ends up killing the priest in revenge.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.080
After killing the priest, Sersi flees to Wakanda.&nbsp;
Dane talks her into coming back, but upon her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:40.880
return, she inexplicably attacks the Avengers.&nbsp;
She is eventually defeated by an imposter of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:46.400
the Vision who has been sent to infiltrate the&nbsp;
team. It turns out that Anti-Vision is one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:51.920
the Gatherers, whose leader, the mysterious&nbsp;
Proctor, is hellbent on terrorizing Sersi.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:57.280
Sersi's fellow Eternals Ikaris, Arex,&nbsp;
and Sprite arrive and demand the Avengers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:02.240
hand Sersi over to them. Ikaris says she is&nbsp;
suffering from a form of insanity found in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:07.600
Eternals called the Mahd Wy'ry, and that it&nbsp;
was probably caused by her use of the Uni-Mind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:12.240
Now, her fellow Eternals plan to take her&nbsp;
home to Olympia and have her "cleansed,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:17.520
which means disintegrating her at a molecular&nbsp;
level — the Eternal equivalent of execution.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:21.360
The Avengers don't like the sound of this,&nbsp;
and a short fight ensues, only ending when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:26.080
Sprite reads Sersi's mind and realizes she is in&nbsp;
love with Dane. Without asking his permission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:31.440
Ikaris bonds Dane to Sersi as her Gann Josin,&nbsp;
or soulmate. Dane, who had just made a move on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:36.600
Crystal, is forced into following a terrifying&nbsp;
imperative: Be with Sersi, or let her die.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:42.000
Sersi's life continues to spiral out of&nbsp;
control, especially after she is connected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.400
to the deaths of two detectives. And when the&nbsp;
police arrive to arrest her for the killings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.640
she responds by leveling Avengers Mansion&nbsp;
and destroying the Brooklyn Bridge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:54.240
Dane remains by her side, forced by&nbsp;
their bond into standing with her...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:59.760
until Sersi goes after Crystal, that is. Only then&nbsp;
does Dane realize that she needs to be stopped.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:04.880
At this point, the enigmatic Proctor captures&nbsp;
her and reveals himself as the Dane Whitman of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:09.360
an alternate universe. He was rejected by the&nbsp;
Sersi of his world, so he made it his mission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:15.200
to drive her insane in every other reality,&nbsp;
using powers stolen from a Watcher. At last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:19.360
Sersi knows her erratic behavior is not&nbsp;
her fault — but the damage has been done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:24.080
regardless. Sersi kills him with his own&nbsp;
Ebony Blade and exiles herself to another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:29.280
dimension. The Dane of her world, his own mind&nbsp;
cleared by Proctor's death, opts to join her.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.920
Sersi and Dane enter the&nbsp;
Ultraverse of Malibu Comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:37.440
home to an alternate Earth and a&nbsp;
whole other cast of superheroes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:42.080
The journey has the desired effect, as Sersi&nbsp;
is able to exist dimensions away from Proctor's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:47.200
control and so finally comes to her senses.&nbsp;
That clarity doesn't last long, unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:52.720
as she is immediately possessed by a heretofore&nbsp;
unknown Infinity Gem called the Ego Gem.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.240
Subsequently, the other Infinity Gems&nbsp;
are transported to the Ultraverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.560
along with the trickster god Loki.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.840
"Surprise."

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:06.480
Loki obtains the other six Gems, and the possessed&nbsp;
Sersi sends a superhero team called Ultraforce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:11.760
led by Dane, after him. When the Grandmaster&nbsp;
travels to the Ultraverse to seek his old Mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:17.440
Gem, he proposes a contest to Loki. His pawns&nbsp;
will be the Avengers, zapped to the Ultraverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:22.080
while Loki's team will be Ultraforce. Loki&nbsp;
wins, but it turns out that this was all a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:27.680
ruse for Sersi to get close enough for the Ego&nbsp;
Gem to reunite with the other legendary stones.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:31.520
The Gem becomes a sentient,&nbsp;
godlike being named Nemesis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:36.640
Nemesis combines the two universes but can't quite&nbsp;
hold them together, and is ultimately defeated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:42.160
when Dane cuts off her crown with the Ebony&nbsp;
Blade. That splits the Gems apart once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:46.400
reconstitutes the Ultraverse, and gives&nbsp;
Dane and Sersi the chance to return home.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.720
When they return to Earth, Sersi and&nbsp;
Dane don't arrive in the present day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:54.160
Instead, they find themselves&nbsp;
in the midst of the Crusades.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:58.800
Dane's mind winds up in the body of a&nbsp;
Crusader ancestor named Eobar Garrington,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:03.760
and it takes Sersi convincing Eobar's spirit&nbsp;
to move on before Dane can assert himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:09.040
Eobar's best friend and fellow Crusader, Bennet&nbsp;
du Paris, isn't pleased about all this, as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:14.320
pair had been on their way to find the Eternal&nbsp;
Pharoah in his Tower of Power. Dane's accidental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:20.080
takeover of Eobar's body spells the end of that&nbsp;
quest, angering Bennet, who goes on by himself.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:26.080
Bennet is then found by the Pharaoh, who turns&nbsp;
out to be the mutant supervillain Apocalypse.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:29.120
"I… have returned."

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:35.120
He activates Bennet's latent mutant powers,&nbsp;
and Bennet becomes the powerful telepath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:40.640
Exodus. Apocalypse orders him to kill Dane and&nbsp;
Sersi, but he refuses to kill his old friend. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:46.000
as punishment, Apocalypse strips him of his powers&nbsp;
and traps him in suspended animation for the next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:52.480
900 years. Exodus would later be freed by Magneto&nbsp;
in an X-Factor storyline from the early '90s.

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:56.160
In the end, Sersi and Dane manage&nbsp;
to return to their rightful time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.160 --> 00:09:01.040
albeit once again in different places. The&nbsp;
trip tears apart their Gann Josin link, too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.800
and Sersi and Dane decide to split up for good.

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:10.000
Left with nowhere else to go, Sersi returns to&nbsp;
Olympia. At the time, Apocalypse is busy turning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:15.120
Deviants into mindless monsters who have begun&nbsp;
attacking humans, and so the Eternals pose as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:20.560
a new team of superheroes called the New Breed.&nbsp;
Joining them, Sersi takes the code-name Mesmer.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:24.960
This lasts until the mischievous Eternal&nbsp;
known as Sprite pulls his ultimate prank in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.920
the lead-up to the 2006 Eternals series:&nbsp;
Erasing the memories of every Eternal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:33.280
As a result, Sersi becomes a&nbsp;
mild-mannered party planner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:38.720
ignorant of her powers and origin. When one of&nbsp;
her parties is attacked by terrorists, Makkari,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:43.920
her former lover and fellow Eternal, helps stop&nbsp;
them. Iron Man then shows up to question Makkari,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:49.360
who is living an amnesiac life as Mark Curry.&nbsp;
Stark recognizes Sersi as a former Avenger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:53.920
but is shocked to discover that there is no&nbsp;
record of her in any of the team's files.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:59.040
As it turns out, this is all a Deviant ruse,&nbsp;
designed to awaken the Dreaming Celestial,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:03.200
who had been banished to Earth for speaking&nbsp;
out against the abuse of Deviants. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:08.080
Makkari convinces the Dreaming Celestial to wait&nbsp;
fifty years before passing judgement on Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:13.200
Sersi decides to give up superheroics once and&nbsp;
for all. She goes back to her party planning job,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:17.840
and other than occasionally advising the&nbsp;
Avengers, keeps her promise to stay retired.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:23.520
In 2018's Avengers #1, the bodies of dead&nbsp;
Celestials begin raining down on Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:27.600
Who could have killed these omnipotent&nbsp;
beings so easily? As it turns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:32.000
it was the Final Host of Dark Celestials,&nbsp;
ready to wipe out the Earth for good.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:36.960
The Avengers learn that the Celestials serve&nbsp;
a transcendent being called the Fulcrum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:42.000
and their job is to not only experiment on young&nbsp;
worlds, but to destroy them after millions of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:47.680
years in order to reap their energy. The Fulcrum&nbsp;
also created a race of insect creatures called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:53.280
the Horde, and the Dark Celestials came about&nbsp;
when the Horde infected a number of Celestials.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:57.680
The Eternals learn that their true purpose&nbsp;
wasn't to protect humanity after all, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:03.600
to cultivate them like crops for the good of the&nbsp;
Celestials. This realization drives them all mad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:07.200
leading to each of their deaths.&nbsp;
Thanks to Ikaris' last words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:11.600
Iron Man is able to determine a way for&nbsp;
humans to form the Uni-Mind. He is then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:17.040
told that something in human DNA can stop the&nbsp;
Horde, and the Avengers manage to save the day.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:21.760
Some time later, Sersi and her fellow Eternals&nbsp;
are resurrected by the machines that give their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:27.120
kind their immortality. After a short conflict&nbsp;
with Thanos, however, Ikaris discovers another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:31.120
horrifying truth behind their existence:&nbsp;
essentially, that a human being is killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:36.240
every time an Eternal is resurrected. Ikaris&nbsp;
decides this process is pretty much unacceptable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:41.600
and he, Sersi, and their fellow Eternals set&nbsp;
out to solve the problem once and for all.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.000
